==========================================================================
I. REVERSAL INVOLUTION:  h*_k = (a_d/a_0) h_{d-k}  and  R*_k = R_{d-k}
==========================================================================
  (n+1)^4(n+2)^4                     d=8  h*_k=(a_d/a_0)h_(d-k): True   R*_k=R_(d-k): True
  distinct 1,2,5,7,11                d=5  h*_k=(a_d/a_0)h_(d-k): True   R*_k=R_(d-k): True
  rational mix                       d=6  h*_k=(a_d/a_0)h_(d-k): True   R*_k=R_(d-k): True
  THM-2991 control (1,1,3,20,20)     d=5  h*_k=(a_d/a_0)h_(d-k): True   R*_k=R_(d-k): True
  non-real-rooted n^4+n^3+3n^2+n+1   d=4  h*_k=(a_d/a_0)h_(d-k): True   R*_k=R_(d-k): True
  VERDICT I: EXACT INVOLUTION

==========================================================================
II. REVERSAL-CLOSURE OF EVERY STANDARD HYPOTHESIS CLASS
==========================================================================
  reversal maps roots r -> 1/r, so:
   * positive coefficients      : reversal permutes the coefficients      -> closed
   * all roots real and negative: 1/r stays real and negative             -> closed
   * PF-infinity                : ASWE = product of (1+r t), r>0; 1/r>0   -> closed
   * Hurwitz stable             : Re(root)<0 <=> Re(1/root)<0             -> closed
   * strict ULC                 : h*_k = c h_(d-k), log-concavity is      -> closed
                                  reversal-symmetric

  (n+1)^4(n+2)^4          : reversal == reciprocal-root poly (up to scalar) True;  PF3 both True;  strict ULC both True
  (n+1)^2(n+3)(n+20)^2    : reversal == reciprocal-root poly (up to scalar) True;  PF3 both True;  strict ULC both True
  (n+1)(n+2)(n+4)(n+8)    : reversal == reciprocal-root poly (up to scalar) True;  PF3 both True;  strict ULC both True

  ONE-LINE NO-GO.  Let H be reversal-closed and suppose every N in H had
  R_k >= R_(k-1) for all k.  For N in H also N* in H, so R*_k >= R*_(k-1),
  i.e. R_(d-k) >= R_(d-k+1), i.e. R_j >= R_(j+1).  Both give R_j = R_(j+1)
  for every j: the ratio sequence is CONSTANT.  Any H containing one member
  with a non-constant ratio sequence therefore cannot imply no-return.
  VERDICT II: ALL LISTED CLASSES ARE REVERSAL-CLOSED

