==========================================================================
IV. RECIPROCAL-CLOSED-UP-TO-SCALAR ROOTS  =>  R_k = R_(d-k) EXACTLY
==========================================================================
  R_k is invariant under r -> lambda r (h_k -> lambda^k h_k cancels), so if
  the root multiset equals lambda * {1/r} for some lambda>0 then R*_k=R_k,
  and with I this gives R_k = R_(d-k).
  (n+1)^4(n+2)^4: R_k=R_(d-k) exactly True;  rises k<= 4;  first fall k=5 (= m+1 = 5);  monotone? False
  (n+1)^6(n+3)^6: R_k=R_(d-k) exactly True;  rises k<= 6;  first fall k=7 (= m+1 = 7);  monotone? False
  (n+2)^8(n+5)^8: R_k=R_(d-k) exactly True;  rises k<= 8;  first fall k=9 (= m+1 = 9);  monotone? False
  (n+1)^10(n+10)^10: R_k=R_(d-k) exactly True;  rises k<= 10;  first fall k=11 (= m+1 = 11);  monotone? False
  (n+3)^5(n+7)^5: R_k=R_(d-k) exactly True;  rises k<= 5;  first fall k=6 (= m+1 = 6);  monotone? False
  => the simplest non-degenerate real-rooted positive family already has
     an EXACT interior maximum: full no-return is impossible on it.
  VERDICT IV: EXACT PALINDROMY

